import Mathlib

/-!
# Motivic structures in the cohomology of moduli of curves: target signatures

The roadmap is `README.md`; this file is not the roadmap. It is the acceptance test: it states,
against the pinned Mathlib and Tau Ceti, those headline theorems of the roadmap that are statable
there. At the pins none is, so the file states nothing; this docstring records each headline
theorem and what it lacks.

The headline theorems are:

* odd cohomology of every moduli stack of stable pointed curves `M̄_{g,n}` vanishes in degrees at
  most nine (README §9.8; Bergström–Faber–Payne, Theorem 1.1);
* `M̄_{4,n}` has polynomial point count, with the explicit polynomials, and pure Tate cohomology,
  for `n ≤ 3` (README §§9.5 and 9.7; Bergström–Faber–Payne, Theorem 1.4);
* for each degree `k`, the semi-tautological extension generated by finitely many explicit groups
  `H^{k′}(M̄_{g′,n′})` contains `H^k(M̄_{g,n})` for all `g, n`, so only finitely many simple Hodge
  structures or Galois representations occur in degree `k` (README §§4.9 and 4.11;
  Canning–Larson–Payne, Theorem 1.3 and Corollary 1.4);
* `H⁴(M̄_{g,n})` is tautological for all `g, n`, `H⁶(M̄_{g,n})` for `g ≥ 10`, and even homology of
  degree at most fourteen is tautological (README §§10.2–10.4; Canning–Larson–Payne, Theorem 1.5);
* homology of degree thirteen, respectively fifteen, lies in the semi-tautological extension
  generated by `H¹¹(M̄_{1,11})`, respectively by `H¹¹(M̄_{1,11})` and `H¹⁵(M̄_{1,15})`
  (README §§12.1–12.2; Canning–Larson–Payne, Theorems 1.6 and 1.7);
* `M_{7,n}` has the Chow–Künneth generation property and tautological rational Chow ring for
  `n ≤ 3` (README §7.7; Canning–Larson–Payne, Theorem 1.10);
* `H¹³(M̄_{g,n})^ss` is a sum of copies of `L S₁₂`, `H¹⁴(M̄_{g,n})^ss` a sum of copies of `L⁷`, and
  for `g ≥ 2` `H¹⁵(M̄_{g,n})^ss` a sum of copies of `L² S₁₂`, as Hodge structures and as `ℓ`-adic
  Galois representations (README §12.9; Canning–Larson–Payne, Theorem 1.1);
* the cohomology of `M̄_{3,n}` for `n ≤ 11` is a polynomial in `L` and `S₁₂` (README §12.10;
  Canning–Larson–Payne, Theorem 1.9).

None of these is statable at the pins. Each needs the moduli stacks `M̄_{g,n}` and `M_{g,n}` of
stable pointed curves; neither Mathlib nor Tau Ceti has algebraic or Deligne–Mumford stacks, stable
curves or their moduli. The cohomological statements also need the rational Betti cohomology of
these stacks with its mixed Hodge structure and their `ℓ`-adic cohomology with its Galois action,
together with the forgetful and clutching morphisms acting on them; the point counts need the
groupoid of rational points of a stack over a finite field; and the Chow statements need rational
Chow groups of stacks and the tautological classes `ψ_i`, `κ_a`. None of these carriers exists at
the pins, and stating the theorems through stand-ins for them would not test the roadmap.
-/

namespace TauCetiRoadmap.MotivicStructuresInModuliOfCurves

end TauCetiRoadmap.MotivicStructuresInModuliOfCurves
